The `source_artifacts` array returned by `sourceArtifactEntries` is not sorted by its `id` field. To prevent diff churn and ensure deterministic ordering, we should strictly order the generated JSON array by its `id` field.

```javascript
  return entries
    .map(([id, role, relPath]) => {
      const target = resolvePath(root, relPath);
      const exists = Boolean(target && fs.existsSync(target));
      const json = readJsonMaybe(root, relPath);
      return {
        id,
        role,
        path: relPath,
        exists,
        schema_version: json?.schema_version ?? null,
        issue: json?.issue ?? null,
        parent_issue: json?.parent_issue ?? null,
        sha256: exists ? sha256File(root, relPath) : null,
      };
    })
    .sort((left, right) => compareByteOrder(left.id, right.id));
```

